From 7e6e3f42daee5fd538dac1dbce83505a2e05926a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: test <test@local>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 08:43:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.60: #[rustc_cxx_throws] attribute scaffolding (1.12
 throws Phase 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Registers the `#[rustc_cxx_throws]` attribute that will drive
LLVM `invoke` lowering for `extern "C++"` calls in P09.61
(Itanium catch landingpad) and P09.62 (MSVC funclet
catchpad/catchswitch). This patch ships only the attribute
recognition layer: parser, HIR variant, cross-crate encoding,
check-attr allowlist, and a CodegenFnAttrFlags::CXX_THROWS
flag that the next patches inspect to decide which call sites
get rewritten from `call` to `invoke`.

Why scaffolding-only here: the codegen invoke lowering is a
substantial chunk on its own (~300 LoC across rustc_codegen_ssa
+ rustc_codegen_llvm), and splitting it from the attribute plumbing
keeps each patch's review surface tight and lets the cxx_importer
side ship the v1.12.5 runtime crate (cxx::native_invoke) against
a stable attribute name immediately.

Plumbing (mirrors P09.48's rustc_swift_throws):

- compiler/rustc_span/src/symbol.rs: +rustc_cxx_throws symbol.
- compiler/rustc_feature/src/builtin_attrs.rs: register the attr.
- compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs:
  AttributeKind::RustcCxxThrows(Span) variant.
- compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/encode_cross_crate.rs: travels
  across crates (Yes).
- compiler/rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs: included in the
  accept-without-target-check allowlist.
- compiler/rustc_attr_parsing/src/attributes/codegen_attrs.rs:
  RustcCxxThrowsParser via the P09.43 rustcc_noargs_attr! macro,
  allowed on Target::ForeignFn.
- compiler/rustc_attr_parsing/src/context.rs: register the parser.
- compiler/rustc_middle/src/middle/codegen_fn_attrs.rs:
  CodegenFnAttrFlags::CXX_THROWS = 1 << 20.
- compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/codegen_attrs.rs: set the flag
  on the callee's CodegenFnAttrs when the attr is present.

User-facing shape (codegen-side activation lands in P09.61):

```rust
unsafe extern "C++" {
    #[rustc_cxx_throws]
    #[link_name = "_Z9do_dividei i"]
    fn do_divide(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32;
}

// After P09.61, the visible signature becomes:
//   fn do_divide(a: i32, b: i32) -> Result<i32, ::cxx::CxxException>
// and call sites lower to LLVM `invoke` with an Itanium catch
// landingpad that calls __rustcc_cxx_catch_unknown.
```

Validation:

- This patch alone does not change codegen behavior; the attribute
  is accepted by the parser and round-trips through HIR + the
  codegen_fn_attrs layer, but no consumer reads CXX_THROWS yet.
- P09.61 / P09.62 will use the flag to gate `call → invoke`
  rewriting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
